1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:03,199
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,199 --> 00:00:05,160
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,960
This is my little brother,
George

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,080
[SNORTS]
This is Mommy Pig.

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,280
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,760
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,320
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,680
Peppa Pig.

9
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,920
[SNORTS]

10
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,880
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:23,360
NARRATOR:
This is Granddad Dog's garage.

12
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,840
[HONKS]

13
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,160
Here are Peppa and her family
in their car.

14
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,720
[SNORTS]
Hello, Danny.

15
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,439
[BARKS]
Hello, Peppa.

16
00:00:30,439 --> 00:00:32,559
[BARKS]
What can we do for you today?

17
00:00:32,559 --> 00:00:35,480
We've got petrol,
air for tires

18
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:38,519
and a new
automatic car wash.

19
00:00:38,519 --> 00:00:41,800
Uh, two ice lollies please.

20
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,800
Oh. Certainly.

21
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,480
Granddad Dog's garage
sells lots of things,

22
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,720
even ice lollies. 
[BOTH GIGGLING]

23
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,080
Thank you. Goodbye.

24
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,720
BOTH: Goodbye.
[HORN HONKS]

25
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,800
[♪♪]

26
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,440
I love our car.

27
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:58,800
[LAUGHS]
And our car loves us too.

28
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,160
Don't you?
[HORN HONKS]

29
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,440
[ALL LAUGHING]

30
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,519
[ENGINE SPUTTERS]

31
00:01:06,039 --> 00:01:08,360
Oh, dear.
The car has stopped.

32
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,720
[ENGINE STALLING]

33
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:12,520
It's no good.
It won't start.

34
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,759
I know.

35
00:01:13,759 --> 00:01:15,280
I'll ring Granddad Dog.

36
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,720
[DIALING]

37
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,000
[RINGING]

38
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,399
Granddad Dog speaking.

39
00:01:21,399 --> 00:01:24,080
Help.
Our car has broken down.

40
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:27,560
Danny, we've got
some rescuing to do.

41
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,640
Yippee!

42
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:32,000
[BARKS]
To the rescue!

43
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,360
To the rescue!

44
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,720
[HORN HONKS]

45
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:37,039
[HORN HONKS]
[SNORTS]

46
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:40,039
Look, there's Danny
and Granddad Dog.

47
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:41,920
ALL:
Hooray!

48
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,479
Granddad Dog knows everything
about cars.

49
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:45,839
Hmm.

50
00:01:45,839 --> 00:01:47,039
Is it serious?

51
00:01:47,039 --> 00:01:50,679
No. You've just run out
of petrol.

52
00:01:50,679 --> 00:01:51,960
What can we do?

53
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,320
There's plenty of petrol
at my garage.

54
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,119
I'll tow you there.

55
00:01:56,119 --> 00:01:58,600
Granddad Dog is towing
Peppa's car

56
00:01:58,600 --> 00:01:59,919
back to his garage.

57
00:01:59,919 --> 00:02:01,360
[HORN HONKS]

58
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:06,160
[♪♪]

59
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:10,799
Granddad Dog is filling
Peppa's car with petrol.

60
00:02:10,799 --> 00:02:13,760
Thank you, Granddad Dog.
[HORN HONKS]

61
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,799
Here are Suzy Sheep
and her mommy in their car.

62
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:18,280
[BLEATS]
Hello, Peppa.

63
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,880
[SNORTS]
Hello, Suzy.

64
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,799
We ran out of petrol.

65
00:02:21,799 --> 00:02:24,280
Granddad Dog rescued us.

66
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:27,000
Wow! That's exciting.

67
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,239
See you later.
See you later.

68
00:02:30,239 --> 00:02:32,280
[GIGGLING]

69
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,000
[TIRE POPS]
[AIR HISSES]

70
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,320
Oh, no.

71
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:40,000
All the air has gone out
of the tire.

72
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,720
Will Granddad Dog
have to rescue us?

73
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,320
I think so.

74
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:46,239
[RINGING]

75
00:02:46,239 --> 00:02:47,880
Granddad Dog speaking.

76
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:49,079
I see.

77
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:50,600
Don't panic,
Mommy Sheep,

78
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,840
I'm on my way.

79
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,000
To the rescue!

80
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,320
Can I go too?

81
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,760
Hop aboard, Peppa.

82
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,120
To the rescue!

83
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,320
[GIGGLING]

84
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,200
To the rescue!

85
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,480
[HORN HONKS]

86
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,560
[HORN HONKS]

87
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,560
Hello, Suzy.
We've come to rescue you.

88
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,200
BOTH:
Hooray!

89
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,880
[♪♪]

90
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:17,160
Granddad Dog
is filling the tire with air.

91
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,519
[AIR HISSING]

92
00:03:19,519 --> 00:03:22,440
Thank you, Granddad Dog.
[HORN HONKS]

93
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:25,239
Here are Granny Pig
and Grandpa Pig in their car.

94
00:03:25,239 --> 00:03:27,120
Hello, everyone.

95
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,320
Hello, Grandpa Pig.

96
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,840
Would you like
some petrol or air?

97
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:35,119
No, thanks. I want
to try out your new carwash.

98
00:03:35,119 --> 00:03:36,280
Certainly.

99
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:38,840
It's run by a computer.
[BEEPS]

100
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:42,320
COMPUTER:
Hello. I am the carwash
of the future.

101
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,040
ALL:
Ooh!

102
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:46,799
First, soapy water.

103
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,840
Then a rinse.

104
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:54,519
And finally, a polish.

105
00:03:54,519 --> 00:03:57,079
ALL:
Wow!

106
00:03:57,079 --> 00:03:59,480
Sorry, I have malfunctioned.

107
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,079
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.
The computer has broken.

108
00:04:02,079 --> 00:04:04,839
And Grandpa Pig's car
is stuck.

109
00:04:04,839 --> 00:04:07,839
Aah! Do something,
Granddad Dog!

110
00:04:07,839 --> 00:04:11,519
Oh. I don't know
how to mend computers.

111
00:04:11,519 --> 00:04:14,600
My daddy mended our computer
at home.

112
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:18,440
Uh, well, I didn't really
mend the computer, I just...

113
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:21,719
Good. Then this is a job
for Daddy Pig.

114
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:23,760
Hmm.

115
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:26,800
Maybe if I just
switch if off.

116
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:30,599
And then switch it on again.

117
00:04:30,599 --> 00:04:33,320
Daddy Pig has mended
the car wash.

118
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,080
ALL:
Hooray!

119
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:38,719
Granddad Dog is the best
at mending cars.

120
00:04:38,719 --> 00:04:41,760
But my daddy
mended the carwash.

121
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,840
[ALL LAUGHING]

122
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:50,760
[♪♪]

123
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,919
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

124
00:04:52,919 --> 00:04:54,159
[BOTH GIGGLING]

125
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:55,719
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George

126
00:04:55,719 --> 00:04:58,000
are going to the playground
today.

127
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,120
Should we drive
to the playground?

128
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,320
No, let's walk.

129
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:04,320
Look. It's just over there.

130
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,200
The playground
is quite close.

131
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,599
[♪♪]

132
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:10,479
[LAUGHS]
Okay, let's walk.

133
00:05:10,479 --> 00:05:12,200
[SNORTS]
This way, everyone.

134
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,400
[BOTH GIGGLING]

135
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,599
We're going to the playground.
We're going to the playground.

136
00:05:18,599 --> 00:05:20,640
[BOTH GIGGLING]

137
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:26,240
Oh. Where has the sky gone?

138
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,359
[SNORTS]
Don't worry, Peppa.

139
00:05:28,359 --> 00:05:29,560
It's just fog.

140
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,520
[SNORTS]
What's fog?

141
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:34,599
Fog is a cloud
that is on the ground

142
00:05:34,599 --> 00:05:35,960
instead of in the sky.

143
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,039
BOTH:
Ooh.

144
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:42,159
Hmm, it's very thick fog.

145
00:05:42,159 --> 00:05:44,599
PEPPA:
I can't see a thing.

146
00:05:44,599 --> 00:05:47,680
Hmm. Maybe we should
go back home.

147
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:50,719
Yes, we'll go to the playground
another day.

148
00:05:50,719 --> 00:05:52,159
BOTH:
Oh.

149
00:05:52,159 --> 00:05:54,320
It is too foggy
to find the playground,

150
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:57,120
so Peppa and George
have to go back home.

151
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,560
Now, which way is home?

152
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,640
[SNORTS]
Are we lost, Daddy Pig?

153
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,919
[LAUGHS]

154
00:06:02,919 --> 00:06:05,800
Don't worry,
I know exactly where we are.

155
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,599
[SNORTS]
This way.

156
00:06:08,599 --> 00:06:09,840
[GRUNTS]

157
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,440
Who put that tree there?

158
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,520
Daddy Pig has walked
into a tree.

159
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,320
Are you okay,
Daddy Pig?

160
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,440
Yes, I'm fine.

161
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,960
[SNORTS]
This way.

162
00:06:22,039 --> 00:06:25,080
Daddy Pig, do you know
where you're going?

163
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,120
Yes, of course I do.

164
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,440
[SNORTS]
I don't think we'll ever find

165
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,680
our house again.

166
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,359
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

167
00:06:32,359 --> 00:06:36,359
I'm sure we will, Peppa.
We're only in our garden.

168
00:06:36,359 --> 00:06:37,760
[QUACKING]

169
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,719
Oh, it's the ducks.

170
00:06:39,719 --> 00:06:40,840
[QUACKS]

171
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,440
Hello, Mrs. Duck.

172
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,440
Have you lost your pond?

173
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,640
[QUACKS]

174
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,960
We're lost too.

175
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:49,960
We are not lost.
I know exactly where we are.

176
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,159
[SNORTS]

177
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:52,479
See you later, ducks.

178
00:06:52,479 --> 00:06:54,000
Good luck finding your pond.

179
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,200
Whoa!
[LOUD SPLASH]

180
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:56,599
ALL:
Oh!

181
00:06:58,479 --> 00:07:01,000
Daddy Pig has found
the duck pond.

182
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,719
[SNORTS]
That's lucky.

183
00:07:02,719 --> 00:07:05,080
Yes. What a stroke of luck.

184
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,359
[ALL LAUGHING]

185
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:07,440
[QUACKS]

186
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:10,880
Daddy,
Mrs. Duck says thank you.

187
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,080
You're most welcome,
Mrs. Duck.

188
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:15,239
[ALL LAUGHING]
[QUACKING]

189
00:07:19,159 --> 00:07:20,919
Now, let's find our house.

190
00:07:20,919 --> 00:07:24,200
[SNORTS]
I'm sure it's this way.

191
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,719
MOMMY RABBIT:
Hello?

192
00:07:25,719 --> 00:07:27,239
Did you hear something?

193
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:29,760
Yes, I thought
I heard someone say...

194
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,000
Hello?

195
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,280
It's Mommy Rabbit

196
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,560
with Rebecca and Richard.

197
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,680
[SQUEAKS]
Hello, Peppa, we're lost.

198
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:40,080
[SNORTS]
Hello, Rebecca. We're lost too.

199
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:42,640
We wanted to go
to the playground.

200
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:46,760
So did we, but it's too foggy
to get there.

201
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,039
Come on, everyone.

202
00:07:48,039 --> 00:07:50,719
Back to our house
until the fog clears.

203
00:07:50,719 --> 00:07:53,680
Daddy Pig, do you know
where you're going?

204
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,239
Yes, of course I do.

205
00:07:55,239 --> 00:07:57,280
[SNORTS]
This way.

206
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,760
ALL:
Yes, Daddy Pig!

207
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,919
[♪♪]

208
00:08:00,919 --> 00:08:02,239
Ah-ha!

209
00:08:02,239 --> 00:08:04,359
[SNORTS]
I've found our little hill.

210
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:05,760
We'll soon be home.

211
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,840
ALL:
Hooray!

212
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:08,960
[SNORTS]

213
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:12,400
Our house should be
just about here.

214
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,760
Oh!

215
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:15,359
Daddy Pig has found
a ladder.

216
00:08:15,359 --> 00:08:17,280
[SNORTS]
That's strange,

217
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:21,000
we don't have a ladder
in our garden.

218
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,960
Goodness me.

219
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,400
Can you see where we are,
Daddy Pig?

220
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,200
Yes, I can.

221
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,599
[LAUGHS]

222
00:08:28,599 --> 00:08:31,000
Daddy, where are we?

223
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,679
Why don't you have a look.

224
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,799
Okay.

225
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,640
Wow!

226
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:41,360
Wow!
I can see everything again.

227
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,799
The fog is going away.

228
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,000
[PEPPA GIGGLES]

229
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,680
We're at the playground.

230
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,959
BOTH:
Hooray!

231
00:08:46,959 --> 00:08:48,199
Whee!

232
00:08:48,199 --> 00:08:49,920
We're at the playground.

233
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,520
We're at the playground.

234
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:52,720
Whee!

235
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,079
[BOTH GIGGLING]

236
00:08:54,079 --> 00:08:57,360
Seesaw.
Seesaw.

237
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,040
Daddy, Mommy!

238
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:01,840
[LAUGHS]
We're at the playground.

239
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:03,319
Well, that's lucky.

240
00:09:03,319 --> 00:09:05,720
But I thought
we were trying to get home.

241
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,120
So did I.

242
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:10,120
Maybe we did get a bit lost
after all.

243
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,199
[ALL LAUGHING]

244
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,360
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

245
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,880
It is a rainy day,

246
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:28,000
and the school roof
has a hole in it.

247
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,160
Children.

248
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,680
We are going to have
a jumble sale.

249
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:36,520
The money we raise
will pay for a new school roof.

250
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,120
ALL:
Hooray!

251
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:41,920
Everyone has to bring something
for the jumble sale.

252
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,760
[SNORTS]
What should we bring?

253
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,400
You can bring an old toy

254
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,839
or something
you don't use anymore.

255
00:09:47,839 --> 00:09:50,199
[ALL MAKING ANIMAL NOISES]

256
00:09:50,199 --> 00:09:52,920
The parents have arrived
to pick up the children.

257
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:55,040
Home time.
[ALL LAUGHING]

258
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,880
Don't forget your old toys

259
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,439
for the jumble sale
tomorrow.

260
00:09:59,439 --> 00:10:01,079
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

261
00:10:01,079 --> 00:10:03,800
Peppa is choosing a toy
for the jumble sale.

262
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,839
Peppa, have you decided?

263
00:10:05,839 --> 00:10:06,959
Um...

264
00:10:06,959 --> 00:10:09,120
You only have to choose
one toy.

265
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:13,199
Yes, and it will help pay
for a new school roof.

266
00:10:13,199 --> 00:10:14,439
Okay.

267
00:10:14,439 --> 00:10:16,400
I'm going to give...

268
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,000
Mr. Dinosaur.

269
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,439
[CRYING]

270
00:10:20,439 --> 00:10:23,040
Mr. Dinosaur is George's
favorite toy.

271
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:25,319
Peppa, you can't give away
Mr. Dinosaur.

272
00:10:25,319 --> 00:10:26,520
Can't I?

273
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,839
No.
No.

274
00:10:27,839 --> 00:10:29,120
Oh, bother.

275
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,319
Sorry, George.

276
00:10:30,319 --> 00:10:31,560
[GIGGLING]

277
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,040
Dinosaur.

278
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,720
[SNORTS]
Why don't you give

279
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:37,160
your old jack-in-a-box.

280
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,880
[ALL LAUGHING]
Okay.

281
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,400
[SNORTS]
Now, it's your turn, Daddy.

282
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,680
What?

283
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:44,079
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

284
00:10:44,079 --> 00:10:46,880
We must all give something
to the jumble sale.

285
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,800
[SNORTS]
I'm giving this hat,

286
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,959
and George
is giving this ball.

287
00:10:50,959 --> 00:10:52,160
[SNORTING]

288
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,120
So, what shall Daddy give?

289
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,400
[SNORTS]
I know. The television.

290
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,680
Not the telly!

291
00:10:57,680 --> 00:11:00,079
No, it's too useful.

292
00:11:00,079 --> 00:11:01,319
Um...

293
00:11:01,319 --> 00:11:02,600
I know.

294
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,920
Daddy's smelly slippers.

295
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:06,920
[SNIFFS AND COUGHS]

296
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,600
No, too smelly.

297
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,839
[BOTH GIGGLING]

298
00:11:09,839 --> 00:11:12,439
I know. Daddy's old chair.

299
00:11:12,439 --> 00:11:14,319
[SPRINGS CREAKING]

300
00:11:14,319 --> 00:11:16,120
But that's an antique.

301
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:18,360
What does "antique" mean?

302
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:21,120
Antique means it's very old
and valuable.

303
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,680
But you found it
on a rubbish tip, Daddy Pig.

304
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,160
It's worthless.

305
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,560
It'll be worth a lot of money
when I mend it.

306
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,199
You've been saying that
for ages, Daddy Pig.

307
00:11:30,199 --> 00:11:31,600
[ALL LAUGHING]

308
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:32,920
[SNORTS]
I know.

309
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,680
I'll give these lovely socks

310
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:36,000
that Granny Pig made me.

311
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,560
PEPPA: Good.
[DOORBELL RINGS]

312
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,199
[DOORBELL RINGS]

313
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,480
[SNORTING]

314
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,319
I've come to collect
your things

315
00:11:43,319 --> 00:11:44,520
for the jumble sale.

316
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,839
Here they are.
Thank you.

317
00:11:46,839 --> 00:11:48,360
[CREAKING]

318
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:51,600
And would you like
this old chair?

319
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,199
Oh, most generous.

320
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,959
Goodbye.
ALL: Bye.

321
00:11:57,959 --> 00:12:01,439
Mommy, you gave away
Daddy's chair.

322
00:12:01,439 --> 00:12:02,600
Shh. Don't tell him.

323
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,880
He'll never notice.

324
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:06,120
[GIGGLES]

325
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,319
It is the day
of the jumble sale.

326
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:12,600
Hello.
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

327
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,800
Peppa, how about
this chair?

328
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,160
It's a bit rubbish,

329
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,600
but you can chop it up
and use it for firewood.

330
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,199
But it's an antique.

331
00:12:20,199 --> 00:12:21,480
Is it?

332
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:23,800
Daddy said it's worth
lots of money.

333
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,000
Well, I never.

334
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,480
I'd better put the price up.

335
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,719
Bye.

336
00:12:27,719 --> 00:12:29,160
[GIGGLING]

337
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,319
Hello, everyone.

338
00:12:30,319 --> 00:12:31,760
ALL:
Hello, Peppa.

339
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,600
What did you give, Suzy?

340
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:36,000
I gave my nurse's outfit.

341
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,160
I gave my parrot balloon.

342
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,400
I gave my toy monkey.

343
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,000
[MIMICS MONKEY]

344
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

345
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:48,680
[SIGH]
I will miss my jack-in-a-box.

346
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:51,439
Can I buy this jack-in-a-box,
please?

347
00:12:51,439 --> 00:12:54,560
And I'd like
this nurse's outfit.

348
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:57,439
The parrot balloon, please.

349
00:12:57,439 --> 00:12:58,760
[ALL GIGGLING]

350
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:01,959
Mommy, Mommy,
look what we've bought.

351
00:13:01,959 --> 00:13:03,719
All your old toys.

352
00:13:03,719 --> 00:13:05,120
We missed them.

353
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

354
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,800
[SNORTS]
Look what I've bought.

355
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,920
It's an antique chair.

356
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,319
Oh, Daddy Pig.

357
00:13:12,319 --> 00:13:14,280
That's not an antique chair.

358
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,800
It is.
Miss Rabbit just said so.

359
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,520
And it matches
my old one.

360
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,400
Yes, Daddy,
that's because...

361
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,640
Shh, Peppa.

362
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:25,400
...it is your old chair.

363
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:26,599
What?

364
00:13:26,599 --> 00:13:28,560
But Miss Rabbit
has just charged me

365
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:30,040
lots of money for it.

366
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:32,520
Fantastic news,
everybody.

367
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:35,480
We have just raised
all the money we need

368
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,280
for a new school roof.

369
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,040
ALL:
Hooray!

370
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,199
Thank you,
Daddy Pig.

371
00:13:41,199 --> 00:13:42,400
[LAUGHS]

372
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,120
You're most welcome.

373
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:46,199
[ALL LAUGHING]

374
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:51,560
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

375
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:55,079
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family
are at the swimming pool.

376
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,839
Daddy Pig is wearing
his swimming costume.

377
00:13:58,839 --> 00:14:01,520
Mommy Pig is wearing
her swimming costume.

378
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:03,920
Peppa is wearing
her swimming costume.

379
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,319
Hurry up, George.

380
00:14:05,319 --> 00:14:07,800
Everyone's waiting.

381
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,079
George is wearing
his swimming costume.

382
00:14:10,079 --> 00:14:11,400
[BOTH GIGGLING]

383
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,240
Peppa, George,

384
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,319
let Daddy
put on your armbands.

385
00:14:17,199 --> 00:14:20,479
[INHALING THEN BLOWING]

386
00:14:20,479 --> 00:14:21,800
There, George.

387
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:24,199
Your armbands
make you look very grown-up.

388
00:14:24,199 --> 00:14:25,479
[SNORTS]

389
00:14:25,479 --> 00:14:26,680
Now me.

390
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:30,199
[INHALING THEN BLOWING]

391
00:14:30,199 --> 00:14:31,360
[GIGGLES]

392
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,199
Good. Now we can go
in the water.

393
00:14:33,199 --> 00:14:35,280
Hooray!
[SNORTS]

394
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,000
[GIGGLING]

395
00:14:41,199 --> 00:14:43,040
[CRYING]

396
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:45,560
It is George's first time
at the swimming pool.

397
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:49,160
Why don't you put
just one foot in to the water?

398
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,800
[CRIES]

399
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,319
Maybe you should try
the other foot.

400
00:14:53,319 --> 00:14:55,040
[CRYING]

401
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:58,160
Maybe George should try
both feet at the same time.

402
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,000
[SNORTS]
Good idea.

403
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,439
[SPLASHES]

404
00:15:01,439 --> 00:15:03,719
[GIGGLING]

405
00:15:03,719 --> 00:15:04,959
[ALL LAUGHING]

406
00:15:04,959 --> 00:15:06,479
Well done, George.

407
00:15:06,479 --> 00:15:09,360
But you don't need to splash
quite so much.

408
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,040
[GIGGLES]

409
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,000
Here is Rebecca Rabbit

410
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,439
with her little brother,
Richard Rabbit.

411
00:15:16,439 --> 00:15:18,839
[SNORTS] Hello, Rebecca.
[SNORTS]

412
00:15:18,839 --> 00:15:21,000
[SQUEAKS]
Hello, everyone.

413
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,439
[SQUEAKING]

414
00:15:22,439 --> 00:15:25,040
Richard,
hold on to this float

415
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,439
and you can practice
kicking your legs.

416
00:15:27,439 --> 00:15:28,640
[SQUEAKS]

417
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:30,719
[SNORTS]
George, would you like to try

418
00:15:30,719 --> 00:15:32,920
kicking your legs?
[SNORTS]

419
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:35,640
[GIGGLING AND SPLASHING]

420
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:36,760
[LAUGHS]

421
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,479
Very good,
but try not to splash.

422
00:15:39,479 --> 00:15:42,520
[SNORTS]
Big children don't splash.

423
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,000
We're very good at swimming.

424
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,400
When George
and Richard are older,

425
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:51,160
they'll be able to swim like us.
Won't they, Rebecca?

426
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,400
Yes.

427
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,079
[BOTH PANTING]

428
00:15:54,079 --> 00:15:55,400
Oh.

429
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,359
Richard has a toy
watering can.

430
00:15:57,359 --> 00:15:59,760
[SNORTS]
Stop it, Richard.

431
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:02,520
[BOTH GIGGLING]

432
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:06,800
Oh, dear. Richard has dropped
his watering can into the pool.

433
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,319
[SOBS]

434
00:16:09,319 --> 00:16:12,160
[BOTH CRYING]

435
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,439
Mommy!

436
00:16:13,439 --> 00:16:16,280
Sorry, Richard,
I can't reach.

437
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,240
It's too far down.

438
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:19,719
Mommy.

439
00:16:19,719 --> 00:16:21,160
I can't swim underwater.

440
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:24,199
Even I can't swim
underwater.

441
00:16:24,199 --> 00:16:25,400
Hmm.

442
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,959
Please, hold my glasses,
Mommy Pig.

443
00:16:27,959 --> 00:16:30,920
[INHALES]

444
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,839
[GASPING]

445
00:16:38,839 --> 00:16:40,640
ALL: Hooray!
[LAUGHS]

446
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,920
There you go.

447
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,719
[SQUEAKING]

448
00:16:43,719 --> 00:16:46,079
Well done, Daddy Pig.

449
00:16:46,079 --> 00:16:49,280
I am rather good
at swimming underwater.

450
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,400
[ALL LAUGHING]

451
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,000
Huh?

452
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,359
[ALL GIGGLING]

453
00:16:54,359 --> 00:16:57,040
The watering can
is for babies.

454
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,680
[SNORTS]
Can we jump off

455
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:00,479
the diving boards now?

456
00:17:00,479 --> 00:17:01,680
Sorry, Peppa.

457
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:03,839
Diving boards are only
for grown-ups.

458
00:17:03,839 --> 00:17:05,159
Oh?
Oh.

459
00:17:05,159 --> 00:17:06,399
Cheer up, you two.

460
00:17:06,399 --> 00:17:08,280
You can watch me dive.

461
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,599
Silly Daddy.

462
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:11,879
Your tummy is too big.

463
00:17:11,879 --> 00:17:13,879
[LAUGHS]
Nonsense.

464
00:17:13,879 --> 00:17:16,760
I won trophies for my diving
when I was younger.

465
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:19,560
That was quite a long time ago,
Daddy Pig.

466
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:23,119
It's lucky I've kept myself
so fit and strong.

467
00:17:23,119 --> 00:17:25,480
Please, hold my glasses,
Mommy Pig.

468
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,319
[SNORTS]
You'll get a better view

469
00:17:27,319 --> 00:17:29,159
if you watch me
from the side.

470
00:17:29,159 --> 00:17:32,320
Please don't splash us
with water, Daddy.

471
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,919
Of course I won't splash you,
Peppa.

472
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,200
I think I need
a higher board.

473
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,280
Please be careful,
Daddy Pig.

474
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:43,000
Yes, don't splash us, Daddy.

475
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,240
[LAUGHS]

476
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,159
Don't worry, Peppa.

477
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:53,320
Don't splash us with water,
Daddy.

478
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,120
I told you
I wouldn't splash.

479
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,440
[ALL LAUGHING]

480
00:17:58,440 --> 00:17:59,840
Clever, Daddy.

481
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:02,000
Well done, Daddy Pig.

482
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,840
No need for my towel.

483
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:06,680
I've got a special way
of drying myself.

484
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,720
[ALL EXCLAIM]

485
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,520
Daddy Pig has splashed everyone
with water.

486
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,080
Daddy Pig!

487
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,680
Sorry, everyone.

488
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,760
[ALL LAUGHING]

489
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:21,040
[♪♪]

490
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,800
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

491
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,800
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

492
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:26,040
[SNORTING]

493
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,520
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

494
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,000
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

495
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,639
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

496
00:18:31,639 --> 00:18:33,760
[SNORTING]

